module

/-!
# leanSPHINCS's positions, as literal tables

The cells `verify_sig_lean_sphincs` reads its signature off, precomputed from the template
generators (`B1/Sig/SphincsT.lean`, `SphincsTail.lean`: `sCoord`, `fkArms`, `foldArms`,
`codewordT`, `kMsg`, `merkleT`) and checked equal to them by kernel evaluation
(`Fast/SphincsTablesCheck.lean`): the codeword's groups' selector cells and the tree's path bases;
the chain starts from a selector (a step of size `3`, `offTab 3`); the forest keys' chain cells
from their arms' base (`fkOffN`); each coordinate's bases and fold outputs (`SCoord`).
-/

namespace LeanVM.Guest.Fast

@[expose] public section

/-- A coordinate's positions: its base (the super-child's selector), each sub-tree's base (the
first `b + 10`), fold base and two top cells, the top fold's base and its two top cells. -/
